      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Deepen: one-word times",
        "body": "Today we stay on the one-word path only (no haber). Keep the thread: verb = action; conjugate = change for who/when; stem = fixed part; ending = tip.\n\nReview the five clocks as one story: present, imperfect, preterite, future, conditional. The helpful contrast is cantaba (leaves the event open) versus canté (closes it).\n\nPráctica: Write five sentences with fixed frames — today / when I was little / yesterday / tomorrow / if I could — same verb, different time. Name the time and say why it fits.\n\nError común: No te quedes con esta confusión: : «Ayer iba al cine» when you mean you went and finished → «Ayer fui al cine»."
      }
    ],
